11
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
The film stars Charlotte Gainsbourg, Stellan Skarsgård, Stacy Martin, Shia LaBeouf, Christian Slater, Jamie Bell, Uma Thurman,
Jean-Marc Barr, Willem Dafoe, Connie Nielsen, and Mia Goth; both Martin and Goth appeared in their film debut.

12
01:07:38,181 --> 01:07:44,181
Separated into two films, the plot follows Joe (played by Gainsbourg and Martin), a self-diagnosed
"nymphomaniac" who recounts her erotic experiences to a bachelor who helps her recover from an assault.

13
01:13:16,363 --> 01:13:22,363
The narrative chronicles Joe's promiscuous life from adolescence to
adulthood and is split into eight chapters told across two volumes.

14
01:18:54,545 --> 01:19:00,545
The film was originally supposed to be only one complete entry, but, because of its length,
von Trier made the decision to split the project into two separate films.

15
01:24:32,727 --> 01:24:38,727
Nymphomaniac was an international co-production of
Denmark, Belgium, France, and Germany.

16
01:30:10,909 --> 01:30:16,909
The world premiere of the uncut Volume I occurred on 16 February 2014 at the 64th Berlin International Film
Festival, while the uncut Volume II premiered at the 71st Venice International Film Festival.

17
01:35:49,090 --> 01:35:55,090
The world premiere of the Director's Cut took place
in Copenhagen on 10 September 2014.

18
01:41:27,272 --> 01:41:33,272
It was nominated for the 2014 Nordic Council Film Prize.

19
01:47:05,454 --> 01:47:11,454
Nymphomaniac is the third and final installment in von Trier's unofficially
titled Depression Trilogy, following Antichrist and Melancholia.

20
01:52:43,636 --> 01:52:49,636
The film explores themes of bondage, whip, sexuality, masochism, sex therapy.

21
